                <pb facs="0556" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/1599: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-26T14:00:00+07:00">May 26, 1943—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 27—10:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>790. Embassy’s 768, May 24, 3 p.m., special exchange regulations. Adler informs
                    us that the Stabilization Board has tacitly approved the new special exchange
                    regulations for foreign Embassies and consular offices by “taking note” of them
                    and not raising our [<hi rendition="#italic">any</hi>] nation [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">objection</hi>] to them and also by requesting Ministry
                    of Finance to instruct Central Bank to report to the Board monthly exchanges
                    sold to and bought from foreign Embassies and consular offices. In the light of
                    this circumstance and as article 3 has been clarified, we assume that, in the
                    absence of instructions to the contrary and pending the making of other possible
                    arrangements, we may take advantage of new rate which benefits the Government
                    and brings much needed, if only temporary, relief to members of the staff.</p>
                <p>It is understood that British and other foreign diplomatic missions are similarly
                    availing themselves of the new rate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
